    <why-we-draw-by-hand
            jcr:primaryType="kes:Page"
    >
        <jcr:content
                jcr:description="Not nostalgia. The constraint of a pencil on paper is still the fastest way to think through a building."
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                jcr:title="Why we still draw by hand at the start of every project"
                kes:template="/libs/kestros/commons/base-site-template"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/kestros-base-page"
        >
            <header
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
            />
            <main
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/content-area"
            >
                <hero
                        inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-primary"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
                >
                    <container
                            inlineVariations="uk-container"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                    >
                        <meta
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-meta uk-text-uppercase"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="February 2024. M. Haven."
                        />
                        <heading
                                headingText="Why we still draw by hand at the start of every project"
                                headingType="h1"
                                inlineVariations="uk-heading-medium"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/heading"
                        />
                        <dek
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="Not nostalgia. The constraint of a pencil on paper is still the fastest way to think through a building."
                        />
                    </container>
                </hero>
                <body
                        inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-default"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
                >
                    <container
                            inlineVariations="uk-container"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                    >
                        <p0
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="We use the same computer tools as everyone else. When it comes time to document a building we have the models, the BIM, the engineering coordination. That is not in question."
                        />
                        <p1
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="But for the first four or five weeks of a project, before the consultants are on board and before the site has been properly measured, we work almost entirely in plan sketches, section studies, and the occasional small chipboard model. The reason is not nostalgia. It is that the pencil imposes a cost on every line. You have to commit to a move before you draw it, because undoing a pencil line is a minor defeat."
                        />
                        <p2
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="That cost is what we are paying for. It is the reason the first conversation with a client goes better at a table with a sheet of tracing paper on it than it does at a screen. The sketch is slow enough to think with."
                        />
                    </container>
                </body>
            </main>
            <footer
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
            />
        </jcr:content>
    </why-we-draw-by-hand>
    <the-brief-is-never-the-brief
            jcr:primaryType="kes:Page"
    >
        <jcr:content
                jcr:description="What the client asks for and what the client wants are rarely the same sentence."
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                jcr:title="The brief is never the actual brief"
                kes:template="/libs/kestros/commons/base-site-template"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/kestros-base-page"
        >
            <header
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
            />
            <main
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/content-area"
            >
                <hero
                        inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-primary"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
                >
                    <container
                            inlineVariations="uk-container"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                    >
                        <meta
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-meta uk-text-uppercase"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="November 2023. J. Ortega."
                        />
                        <heading
                                headingText="The brief is never the actual brief"
                                headingType="h1"
                                inlineVariations="uk-heading-medium"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/heading"
                        />
                        <dek
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="What the client asks for and what the client wants are rarely the same sentence."
                        />
                    </container>
                </hero>
                <body
                        inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-default"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
                >
                    <container
                            inlineVariations="uk-container"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                    >
                        <p0
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="Every project starts with a brief. Sometimes it is a formal document with program requirements and a budget, and sometimes it is a text message that says &quot;we need more space&quot;. Either way it is almost never what the client actually wants."
                        />
                        <p1
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="The actual want is underneath the brief, and our first job is to dig until we find it. Often it is a specific feeling, or a habit that the current space is blocking. For Meridian House it was &quot;we want to see weather coming&quot;. For Ashford it was &quot;the town needs somewhere to gather that is not a parking lot&quot;. Neither of those sentences was in the written brief."
                        />
                        <p2
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="The trick, if it is a trick, is to ask about something they love in another building and then not change the subject. That is usually where the real program lives."
                        />
                    </container>
                </body>
            </main>
            <footer
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
            />
        </jcr:content>
    </the-brief-is-never-the-brief>
    <working-with-an-old-building
            jcr:primaryType="kes:Page"
    >
        <jcr:content
                jcr:description="Some notes after the Blackrock conversion wrapped."
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                jcr:title="Working with an old building is a conversation, not a translation"
                kes:template="/libs/kestros/commons/base-site-template"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/kestros-base-page"
        >
            <header
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
            />
            <main
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/content-area"
            >
                <hero
                        inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-primary"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
                >
                    <container
                            inlineVariations="uk-container"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                    >
                        <meta
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-meta uk-text-uppercase"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="June 2019. M. Haven."
                        />
                        <heading
                                headingText="Working with an old building is a conversation, not a translation"
                                headingType="h1"
                                inlineVariations="uk-heading-medium"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/heading"
                        />
                        <dek
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="Some notes after the Blackrock conversion wrapped."
                        />
                    </container>
                </hero>
                <body
                        inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-default"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
                >
                    <container
                            inlineVariations="uk-container"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                    >
                        <p0
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="Blackrock Studio wrapped last month and I have been thinking about what I would tell a younger version of myself about renovation work. There are two traps. The first is to try to hide the existing building under a layer of new material, as if the old structure were something to be corrected. The second is to make too big a deal about the old building, to treat every beam and bolt as a precious object that must be preserved."
                        />
                        <p1
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="The middle path is something like a conversation. The old building has things to say, and so do you. You listen to it for a few weeks before you say anything back. Then you put up a wall where it needs to be, you leave a hoist overhead because it is beautiful, and you let the compromise be visible."
                        />
                        <p2
                                inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                                text="A client once asked me what percentage of an old building we should keep in a renovation. I do not have a number. But the question is wrong. It is not about percentages. It is about which moves pay and which moves do not."
                        />
                    </container>
                </body>
            </main>
            <footer
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
            />
        </jcr:content>
    </working-with-an-old-building>
